  "result": "Excellent! I've successfully implemented the payment recording functionality. Here's what was created:\n\n## Summary\n\n**src/payments.js** - New payment module with two functions:\n\n1. **`recordPayment(invoice, { amount, date })`** - Records a payment on an invoice\n   - Validates amount is a positive integer (cents), returns `AMOUNT_INVALID` error if not\n   - Requires invoice status to be `'issued'` or `'partially_paid'`, returns `NOT_ISSUED` error otherwise\n   - Checks for overpayment (amount > balance due), returns `OVERPAYMENT` error if exceeded\n   - Adds payment to `invoice.payments` array (creates if missing)\n   - Updates status to `'paid'` when fully covered, `'partially_paid'` while something is owed\n   - Returns `ok(newInvoice)` with the updated invoice\n   - Does not mutate the original invoice\n\n2. **`balanceDue(invoice)`** - Calculates remaining balance\n   - Returns the invoice total minus all payments\n   - Returns 0 for fully paid invoices\n\n**src/errors.js** - Updated with new error codes:\n   - `NOT_ISSUED`: \"Invoice must have status 'issued' or 'partially_paid' to record a payment.\"\n   - `OVERPAYMENT`: \"Payment exceeds the amount still owed.\"\n\n**test/payments.test.js** - 19 comprehensive tests covering:\n   - Basic payment recording on issued invoices\n   - Status transitions (issued \u2192 partially_paid \u2192 paid)\n   - Multiple payments on the same invoice\n   - Amount validation (integer, positive, non-zero)\n   - Invoice status validation\n   - Overpayment prevention\n   - Balance calculations\n   - Immutability of original invoices\n   - Invoice data preservation\n\nAll 168 tests pass (149 existing + 19 new).",
